alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The layout_oracle entry, invoked as `layout_oracle MODE REPS PAGE UA [SUFFIX=SHEET ...]` with the style oracle's arguments, from the repository root, with the installed fonts copied into build/fonts. It loads the page and its sheets with pkg::oracle::page, computes styles and loads the fonts, then: dump matches the fonts, builds and lays out the page once and writes the format of tests/layout/layout_oracle.mjs to standard output; boxes, text and layout repeat REPS times the stage's parts in nested order, so that the time of each part is the difference between consecutive modes: boxes builds the box tree, text also matches each font group's faces (pkg::layout::text::pick_fonts) and prepares every paragraph's text (font matching, shaping and break opportunities), and layout also lays the tree out; each prints the mode, the element, context and paragraph counts and REPS. nodes (REPS 0) lists the nodes of the document in tree order, without styles or fonts: an element as `E NODE DEPTH NAME DESCENDANTS INDEX` (NODE the node identifier, DEPTH the number of element ancestors, DESCENDANTS the number of elements below it, INDEX its position in the traversal), a Text node as `T NODE PARENT LENGTH DATA` (LENGTH in bytes, DATA with backslash written `\\` and line feed `\n`), and last `N COUNT`, the number of nodes the document holds. edit takes the path of an edit script in place of REPS: it loads the page, applies the script's S lines, runs the whole pipeline (traversal, styles, font matching, layout, placement) on the live document and prints `base hash H bytes N`, H being the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the dump in 16 hexadecimal digits and N its size; then, for each edit line in order, it applies the edit to the live document, reruns the pipeline and prints `edit I hash H bytes N` (I from 1); after a T/D text edit, C/K style edit or B/X structural edit, which it also applies to a layout kept across edits with pkg::layout's text_changed, styles_changed or structure_changed followed by update, the line ends in ` inc same` or ` inc DIFF` as the kept layout's dump is or is not byte for byte the rebuilt one's, or ` inc refused` when text_changed, styles_changed, structure_changed or update refused the edit (a P line's dump of a differing edit is followed by the line `inc dump` and the incremental dump), and the kept layout becomes the rebuilt one after a difference, a refusal or any other edit. Checking also reports style-update work as `style edit I prepared R contexts C paragraphs P held_entries H entries E`, and a B or X edit adds `structure edit I contexts C paragraphs P reused R`, pkg::layout's structure_counts. incremental takes the script as edit does, applies each T/D text edit, C/K style edit and B/X structural edit to the kept layout and prints `edit I us U prepared R contexts C paragraphs P held_entries H entries E`, U the microseconds of text_changed and update for text edits, or layout_changes, font picking, styles_changed or structure_changed and update for style and structural edits (the traversal and the styles are rebuilt outside the interval), and the rest pkg::layout's update_counts, or `edit I inc refused` after rebuilding the layout, and rebuilds it after any other edit, printing `edit I full`. Style recomputation stays outside the timed layout interval; a separate `style edit I delta_us D picks_us P full_us F` line gives the delta and font-picking portions and a full comparator using fresh font picks, build_layout and lay_out on the same edited document and computed styles, excluding style computation and placement. The script has one operation per line: `S CSS` adds the rest of the line as an author style sheet after the page's own, only before the first edit; `T NODE OFFSET TEXT` inserts the rest of the line (with `\\` and `\n` resolved) into a Text node's data at a byte offset; `D NODE OFFSET LENGTH` deletes bytes of a Text node's data; `C ELEMENT TOKEN` and `K ELEMENT TOKEN` add a token to and remove a token from an element's class attribute; `B PARENT BEFORE TEXT` inserts a new HTML p element holding one Text node of the text into PARENT before the node BEFORE (`-` for the end) and prints `created NODE` before the edit's line; `X NODE` detaches a node; `P I` requests the full dump of edit I (0 for the unedited document) after its hash line. The style attributes and presentational hints are recorded once, at load, by NodeId, so they stay with their elements across edits; an element an edit creates has none. Exits 2 when the invocation, a file, the page, the style stage, the layout stage or an edit script line fails.";
